# absent-input census -- checks/ and gates/ instruments naming an ABSENT external or own-directory input
# HEAD 444890672d9baebb6309952495f480623f481fc5; columns:
# instrument \t target \t exists_disk \t exists_HEAD \t guarded \t verdict \t evidence
checks/classify.sh	.agents/slop/mutledger/BLOBHIST.tsv	no	no	no	DEFECT-ABSENT-UNGUARDED	READ	classify.sh:20 `H=.agents/slop/mutledger/BLOBHIST.tsv`; the ONLY use is :26 `grep -q "^$live\t$b\$" "$H"`. absent disk AND HEAD (in 5 commits of history, 5444ea42e and 4 siblings -- RECOVERABLE). The only `[ -f` in the file is :18 (pyproject.toml); there is no test of `$H` and no exit-3 arm for it. grep on a missing file exits 2, so the `else` at :27 fires and EVERY differing file is reported PLANT instead of STALE, and the script's exit status is the last printf = 0. GREEN AND WRONG, which is worse than FAIL. Contradicts its own header (:9-10).
checks/gen_gate.py	hdr.bend	no	no	no	DEFECT-ABSENT-UNGUARDED	READ	gen_gate.py:138 `HEADER = open(os.path.join(HERE, "hdr.bend")).read()` at COLUMN 0 (module level; main() is at :170). absent disk AND HEAD; `git log --all -- checks/hdr.bend` EMPTY (0 commits ever). NO guard of any kind: grep is_file|exists|refuse|exit(3)|SystemExit|FileNotFound|except over the whole file returns NOTHING. FileNotFoundError at import -> CPython exit 1 -> READS AS FAIL. Live consumer: .agents/slop/i64div/gate.sh:15 turns it into `GENERATOR FAILED` exit 1; .agents/slop/i64mul/census.py:18,87 subprocesses it. Already listed as 'libraries (no guard)' in .agents/slop/gatesrun/REPORT.md:22.
